Package: textileCrystR
Type: Package
Title: XRD Crystallinity Determination for Textile Fibres and Cellulose
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jherby Kyle C.", "Teodoro", email = "jherbykyleteodoro17@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-6675-5821"))
Description: A small, reproducible toolkit for X-ray diffraction (XRD)
    crystallinity determination of textile fibres and cellulose materials,
    implementing distinct published methods rather than claiming a single
    "true" crystallinity. The Segal peak-height index reads intensities at
    requested I200 and Iam positions with explicit interpolation; the
    peak-area (deconvolution) method jointly fits crystalline peaks and an
    amorphous hump (Gaussian, Lorentzian, pseudo-Voigt or Voigt profiles) and
    reports crystallinity as the crystalline peak area over the total area.
    Every result is a documented object with print, summary, plot and
    data-frame methods, retaining the positions, intensities or fitted
    parameters used. Literature-supported position presets, a robustness
    (sensitivity) analysis over a grid of Segal positions, input validation
    and an experimental cotton validation data set are included. A one-shot
    wrapper reads a file and produces a result and plot in a single call, and
    an optional interactive Shiny dashboard supports both methods across
    multiple uploaded files and samples, either tuned live one sample at a
    time or analyzed as a batch. Methods are treated throughout as empirical
    and are never averaged into one crystallinity value (Segal et al.
    (1959); Nam et al. (2016) <doi:10.1016/j.carbpol.2015.08.035>; Salem et
    al. (2023) <doi:10.1039/D2CS00569G>).
